; nfca_card.loom
; An ISO/IEC 14443 Type A card (PICC, NFC-A, 106 kbit/s) at baseband, with a
; single-size (4-byte) UID: it reads the reader's modified Miller pauses,
; answers REQA and WUPA with ATQA, answers the cascade level 1 ANTICOLLISION
; with the rest of its UID only when the reader's prefix (NVB bytes and bits)
; matches its own, and answers SELECT with SAK and CRC_A. A prefix or a UID
; that is not its own leaves it silent.
;
; Written on 2026-11-26, after the hardware was complete (D-032), as a
; protocol Loom was not designed for (D-035). Nothing in Loom was built for
; NFC. The program times the reader's pauses with the level waits (`WAITP`,
; built for I2C and SPI, the deadline timeout `T` as the end of a frame) and
; reads of the `NOW` tick counter (the deadline timebase, SEMANTICS 4). It
; makes the 847.5 kHz subcarrier with the deadline-latched pin write
; (`SETP ... D`, 6.10, built for exact edges) on a tick of half a subcarrier
; period, a fractional tick (TICK_FRAC, built for UART baud rates) written
; at run time, so the subcarrier keeps fc/16 on average at any clock. Its
; tables live in the data memory (`LD`/`ST`, 6.11, built for device
; emulation). What the firmware does that no hardware does: the modified
; Miller decoder, the Manchester-on-subcarrier coder, the odd parity, CRC_A,
; the frame delay time and the card's states.
;
; Baseband only: there is no 13.56 MHz carrier and no RF. ENV = IN0 is the
; reader's field as a logic level, high = carrier on, low = a pause (100 %
; ASK). LM = OUT0 is the load modulation switch: high = loaded. The
; subcarrier is on-off keyed onto LM; a front end makes the field and loads
; the coil.
;
; Sources (tools/protomodels/iso14443a.py cites them item by item): NXP
; MFRC522 data sheet Rev. 3.9 (Table 4: 106 kBd = 100 % ASK modified Miller
; one way, subcarrier fc/16 Manchester load modulation the other, bit 128/fc;
; Figure 6: start bit, 8 data bits, odd parity; Tables 49/50: CollPos;
; Table 56: CRC preset 6363h). Proxmark3 armsrc/iso14443a.c (sequences X, Y,
; Z, D, E, F; start Z, end logic 0 then Y; the answer 1172 or 1236 carrier
; periods after the reader; SEL 93h, NVB, BCC, SAK cascade bit 04h). libnfc
; iso14443-subr.c (CRC_A). The ISO text is paywalled: what no source above
; states is marked "from memory, unchecked" in the model.
;
; Receiving (tick 1 clock). Pauses start on the half-bit grid: Z at a bit's
; start, X at its middle, and all have one length, so they are timed by
; their rises (stamped at once, decoded after: a decode can outlast a
; pause, never the 2 halves to the next rise). From one rise to the next is
; 2, 3 or 4 half bits: thresholds 2.5 and 3.5 halves (5T/4, 7T/4), a
; margin of half a half bit (118 clocks at 50 MHz). With the parity of
; the last pause's position (even = Z, odd = X): even + 2 -> 0, even + 3 ->
; 1, odd + 2 -> 1, odd + 3 -> 0 0, odd + 4 -> 0 1; even + 4 (a Y after a 0)
; is illegal and drops the frame. No pause within 4.5 halves (9T/4) ends the
; frame; a last pause on an even position was the end's Z, so its 0 is
; dropped. Bits are packed 9 to a word, LSB first: 8 data bits and the odd
; parity at bit 8, as the tables are, so a whole-word compare checks the
; parity too. A frame of 9n + 8 bits (no parity after a whole byte) or over
; 20 words is dropped.
;
; Replying (tick h = 8/fc, half a subcarrier period). A bit is 16 ticks: D
; (1) = subcarrier for 8 ticks then none, E (0) = none then 8 ticks; start D,
; end F (the line stays low). The first rise comes FDT after the rising edge
; of the reader's last pause: 1236/fc if the last pause was an X (last data
; bit 1), 1172/fc if a Z. The next bit is fetched in the half bit without
; subcarrier; the one step with one tick to spare is E followed by D (4
; slots, slack 10 clocks at a 26-clock tick).
;
; Host words (INQ thread 0), after RUN: 1. TICK_INT and 2. TICK_FRAC of h;
; 3. T, the bit in clocks; 4. FDT after a 1 and 5. after a 0, in clocks;
; 6. UID0 | UID1 << 8; 7. UID2 | UID3 << 8; 8. ATQA (sent low byte first);
; 9. SAK. Nothing is reported on OUTQ.
;
; States (this program's reading of ISO/IEC 14443-3, from memory, unchecked):
; IDLE answers REQA and WUPA (then READY); READY answers REQA and WUPA again,
; a matching ANTICOLLISION (stays READY) and a matching SELECT (then ACTIVE);
; anything else leaves READY silent. ACTIVE answers nothing: no HLTA, no
; ISO/IEC 14443-4 (RATS), no MIFARE commands.
;
; Limits, honestly: cascade level 1 only (no 7- or 10-byte UID, no cascade
; tag), 106 kbit/s only, no HALT state. The card's bit grid comes from its
; own clock, not from the reader's carrier as a real card's does; the
; fractional tick keeps the subcarrier within 1 clock of the fc/16 grid.
;
; Memory: RXB = 0x1C0, the received frame (up to 20 words); BASE = 0x1E0:
; +0..+8 the SELECT this card answers (93h 70h UID0..3 BCC CRC_A), +9/+10
; ATQA, +11..+13 SAK and its CRC_A, each byte | parity << 8; +16 5T/4,
; +17 7T/4, +18 9T/4, +19/+20 the FDTs less the lead, +21/+22 TICK_INT /
; TICK_FRAC, +23 the state (0 IDLE, 1 READY, 2 ACTIVE), +24 the last
; pause's rise, +25 the last pause's parity.
;
; Registers, receiving: r1 the last rise, r2 the interval, r3 the parity of
; the last pause, r4 the word pointer, r5 the word, r6 the bit mask, r0/r7
; scratch. Sending: r1 the byte pointer, r2 the word, r3 bits left in it,
; r5 bytes left, r6 the next bit (0, 1, 2 = end), r0/r7 scratch.

        .imem   512                     ; the macro build: quarters of 128 words
        .thread 0
        .pins   ENV = IN0, LM = OUT0

        .equ    HMIN = 26               ; clocks: the shortest h (45 MHz)
        .tick   HMIN
        .equ    RXB = 0x1C0
        .equ    BASE = 0x1E0
        .equ    LAG = 11                ; clocks from the FDT wait to the new grid

        SETP    LM, 0                   ; unloaded
        MOV16   r6, BASE
        POP     r0                      ; 1. TICK_INT of h
        ST      r0, r6, 21
        MOV     r1, r0
        POP     r0                      ; 2. TICK_FRAC of h
        ST      r0, r6, 22
        POP     r0                      ; 3. T
        MOV     r2, r0
        SHRI    r2, 2                   ; T/4
        ADD     r3, r0, r2
        ST      r3, r6, 16              ; 5T/4: 2.5 halves
        MOV     r4, r0
        SHRI    r4, 1
        ADD     r3, r3, r4
        ST      r3, r6, 17              ; 7T/4: 3.5 halves
        ADD     r3, r0, r0
        ADD     r3, r3, r2
        ST      r3, r6, 18              ; 9T/4: the end of a frame
        POP     r0                      ; 4. FDT after a 1
        SUB     r0, r0, r1
        SUBI    r0, LAG
        ST      r0, r6, 19              ; less the lead: h + LAG
        POP     r0                      ; 5. FDT after a 0
        SUB     r0, r0, r1
        SUBI    r0, LAG
        ST      r0, r6, 20
        MOV16   r0, 0x93                ; SEL, cascade level 1
        ST      r0, r6, 0
        LDI     r0, 0x70                ; NVB of a SELECT: 7 bytes, 0 bits
        ST      r0, r6, 1
        POP     r0                      ; 6. UID0 | UID1 << 8
        MOV     r2, r0
        SHLI    r2, 8
        SHRI    r2, 8
        ST      r2, r6, 2
        SHRI    r0, 8
        ST      r0, r6, 3
        XOR     r3, r2, r0              ; BCC = UID0 ^ UID1 ^ UID2 ^ UID3
        POP     r0                      ; 7. UID2 | UID3 << 8
        MOV     r2, r0
        SHLI    r2, 8
        SHRI    r2, 8
        ST      r2, r6, 4
        SHRI    r0, 8
        ST      r0, r6, 5
        XOR     r3, r3, r2
        XOR     r3, r3, r0
        ST      r3, r6, 6
        MOV16   r3, 0x8408              ; x^16 + x^12 + x^5 + 1, reflected
        MOV16   r2, 0x6363              ; CRC_A preset
        MOV     r1, r6
        LDI     r5, 7
cl:     LD      r0, r1, 0
        CALL    crcb
        ADDI    r1, 1
        DJNZ    r5, cl
        MOV     r0, r2
        SHLI    r0, 8
        SHRI    r0, 8
        ST      r0, r6, 7               ; CRC_A, low byte first
        SHRI    r2, 8
        ST      r2, r6, 8
        POP     r0                      ; 8. ATQA
        MOV     r2, r0
        SHLI    r2, 8
        SHRI    r2, 8
        ST      r2, r6, 9
        SHRI    r0, 8
        ST      r0, r6, 10
        POP     r0                      ; 9. SAK
        ST      r0, r6, 11
        MOV16   r2, 0x6363
        CALL    crcb
        MOV     r0, r2
        SHLI    r0, 8
        SHRI    r0, 8
        ST      r0, r6, 12
        SHRI    r2, 8
        ST      r2, r6, 13
        MOV     r1, r6
        LDI     r5, 14
pl:     LD      r0, r1, 0               ; every byte | odd parity << 8
        CALL    par
        ST      r0, r1, 0
        ADDI    r1, 1
        DJNZ    r5, pl
        LDI     r0, 0
        ST      r0, r6, 23              ; IDLE
        JMP     rx

; crcb: r2 = CRC_A updated with the byte r0, LSB first (r3 = 8408h; r4)
crcb:   XOR     r2, r2, r0
        LDI     r4, 8
cb1:    SHRI    r2, 1
        BNC     cb2
        XOR     r2, r2, r3
cb2:    DJNZ    r4, cb1
        RET
; par: r0 = the byte r0 with its odd parity at bit 8 (r3, r4, r7)
par:    MOV     r7, r0
        LDI     r4, 8
        LDI     r3, 1
p1:     SHRI    r7, 1
        BNC     p2
        XORI    r3, 1
p2:     DJNZ    r4, p1
        SHLI    r3, 8
        OR      r0, r0, r3
        RET
; emit: one received bit (e1: a 1, e0: a 0) into r5 at the mask r6; every
; ninth bit stores the word at r4 (r0)
e1:     OR      r5, r5, r6
e0:     SHLI    r6, 1
        MOV     r0, r6
        SHRI    r0, 9
        BZ      eret
        ST      r5, r4, 0
        LDI     r5, 0
        LDI     r6, 1
        MOV     r0, r4
        ANDI    r0, 63
        CMPI    r0, 20
        BC      eret                    ; 20 words: no further
        ADDI    r4, 1
eret:   RET

; ---------------------------------------------------------------- receive
rx:     WAITP   ENV, 1                  ; the field, no pause
        WAITP   ENV, 0                  ; the start of communication (a Z)
        MOV16   r4, RXB
        LDI     r5, 0
        LDI     r6, 1
        LDI     r3, 0                   ; position 0: even
        MOV16   r7, BASE
        WAITP   ENV, 1
        CSRR    r1, NOW                 ; pauses are timed rise to rise
nxt:    ST      r1, r7, 24              ; the last pause's rise
        LD      r0, r7, 18
        ADD     r0, r0, r1
        CSRW    TD, r0                  ; 4.5 halves after the last rise
        WAITP   ENV, 0, T
        BT      fend
        WAITP   ENV, 1
        CSRR    r0, NOW
        SUB     r2, r0, r1              ; rise to rise
        MOV     r1, r0
        LD      r0, r7, 16
        CMP     r2, r0
        BNC     d2                      ; under 2.5 halves: 2
        LD      r0, r7, 17
        CMP     r2, r0
        BNC     d3                      ; under 3.5 halves: 3
        CMPI    r3, 0
        BZ      bad                     ; even + 4: a Y after a 0
        CALL    e0                      ; odd + 4: 0 1
        CALL    e1
        JMP     nxt
d2:     CMPI    r3, 0
        BNZ     d2o
        CALL    e0                      ; even + 2: 0
        JMP     nxt
d2o:    CALL    e1                      ; odd + 2: 1
        JMP     nxt
d3:     XORI    r3, 1
        BZ      d3o
        CALL    e1                      ; even + 3: 1, now odd
        JMP     nxt
d3o:    CALL    e0                      ; odd + 3: 0 0, now even
        CALL    e0
        JMP     nxt
bad:    WAITP   ENV, 1                  ; drop the frame: wait for a quiet line
        LD      r0, r7, 18
        CSRR    r1, NOW
        ADD     r0, r0, r1
        CSRW    TD, r0
        WAITP   ENV, 0, T
        BNT     bad
        JMP     rx

; fend: the frame is over. r3 even: the end's Z made the last 0, drop it.
fend:   ST      r3, r7, 25
        CMPI    r3, 0
        BNZ     fe2
        SHRI    r6, 1
        BNZ     fe2
        SUBI    r4, 1                   ; the 0 was a word's parity bit
        LD      r5, r4, 0
        MOV16   r6, 0x100
fe2:    MOV     r0, r4
        ANDI    r0, 63
        CMPI    r0, 20
        BC      rx                      ; too long: dropped
        ST      r5, r4, 0               ; the partial word (if any)
        LDI     r2, 0                   ; r2 = bits in the last word
fe3:    SHRI    r6, 1
        BZ      fe4
        ADDI    r2, 1
        JMP     fe3
fe4:    CMPI    r2, 8
        BZ      rx                      ; a whole byte with no parity: dropped
        LD      r1, r7, 23              ; the state
        CMPI    r1, 2
        BZ      rx                      ; ACTIVE: silent
        MOV16   r6, RXB
        CMPI    r0, 0
        BNZ     long
        CMPI    r2, 7
        BNZ     rx                      ; a short frame is 7 bits
        LDI     r1, 0x26                ; REQA
        CMP     r5, r1
        BZ      atqa
        LDI     r1, 0x52                ; WUPA
        CMP     r5, r1
        BNZ     rx
atqa:   LDI     r1, 1
        ST      r1, r7, 23              ; READY
        MOV     r1, r7
        ADDI    r1, 9                   ; ATQA: 2 bytes from bit 0
        LDI     r0, 0
        LDI     r5, 2
        JMP     reply

; long: r0 = whole words, r2 = bits in the last, r6 = RXB, r7 = BASE
quiet:  JMP     rx                      ; silent: back to listening
long:   CMPI    r1, 1
        BNZ     quiet                   ; not READY: silent
        MOV     r5, r0
        LD      r3, r6, 0
        LD      r4, r7, 0
        CMP     r3, r4
        BNZ     quiet                   ; not SEL 93h (with its parity)
        CMPI    r5, 2
        BNC     quiet
        LD      r1, r6, 1               ; NVB with its parity bit
        MOV     r0, r1
        SHLI    r0, 8
        SHRI    r0, 8
        CALL    par
        CMP     r0, r1
        BNZ     quiet                   ; a parity error
        MOV     r4, r1
        SHLI    r4, 8
        SHRI    r4, 8                   ; NVB
        MOV16   r7, BASE
        LDI     r3, 0x70
        CMP     r4, r3
        BZ      select
        MOV     r3, r4
        SHRI    r3, 4                   ; bytes, SEL and NVB included
        ANDI    r4, 15                  ; bits
        CMP     r3, r5
        BNZ     quiet                   ; the frame's length is not NVB's
        CMP     r4, r2
        BNZ     quiet
        CMPI    r3, 2
        BNC     quiet
        CMPI    r3, 7
        BC      quiet                   ; NVB 20h .. 67h only
        LDI     r1, 2
acw:    CMP     r1, r3
        BZ      acp
        ADD     r0, r6, r1
        LD      r5, r0, 0
        ADD     r0, r7, r1
        LD      r0, r0, 0
        CMP     r5, r0
        BNZ     quiet                   ; not this card's UID byte
        ADDI    r1, 1
        JMP     acw
acp:    CMPI    r4, 0
        BZ      acm
        ADD     r0, r6, r3              ; the split byte: its first r4 bits
        LD      r5, r0, 0
        ADD     r0, r7, r3
        LD      r0, r0, 0
        XOR     r5, r5, r0
        LDI     r0, 1
        SHL     r0, r0, r4
        SUBI    r0, 1
        AND     r5, r5, r0
        BNZ     quiet
acm:    ADD     r1, r7, r3              ; the rest of UID and BCC from there
        MOV     r0, r4
        LDI     r5, 7
        SUB     r5, r5, r3
        JMP     reply
select: CMPI    r5, 9
        BNZ     quiet
        CMPI    r2, 0
        BNZ     quiet
        LDI     r1, 0
slw:    ADD     r0, r6, r1
        LD      r5, r0, 0
        ADD     r0, r7, r1
        LD      r0, r0, 0
        CMP     r5, r0
        BNZ     quiet                   ; not this card, or a CRC_A error
        ADDI    r1, 1
        CMPI    r1, 9
        BNZ     slw
        LDI     r0, 2
        ST      r0, r7, 23              ; ACTIVE
        MOV     r1, r7
        ADDI    r1, 11                  ; SAK and CRC_A
        LDI     r0, 0
        LDI     r5, 3

; ------------------------------------------------------------------ reply
; In: r1 = the first word, r0 = the first bit in it, r5 = words, r7 = BASE.
reply:  LD      r2, r1, 0
        SHR     r2, r2, r0
        LDI     r3, 9
        SUB     r3, r3, r0              ; bits left in the first word
        LD      r0, r7, 25
        CMPI    r0, 0                   ; the last pause: odd = X, a 1
        LD      r4, r7, 19
        BNZ     rp1
        LD      r4, r7, 20
rp1:    LD      r0, r7, 24
        ADD     r4, r4, r0
        CSRW    TD, r4                  ; FDT after the last rise, less the lead
        LD      r0, r7, 21
        LD      r4, r7, 22
        WAITD   0
        CSRW    TICK_FRAC, r4
        CSRW    TICK_INT, r0            ; the grid restarts here (SEMANTICS 4)
        SETD    0
        SETP    LM, 1, D
        WAITD   1                       ; the start bit's first rise

; D: subcarrier in the first half (entered on its first rise), none after
dbit:   SETP    LM, 0, D
        WAITD   1
        SETP    LM, 1, D
        WAITD   1
        SETP    LM, 0, D
        WAITD   1
        SETP    LM, 1, D
        WAITD   1
        SETP    LM, 0, D
        WAITD   1
        SETP    LM, 1, D
        WAITD   1
        SETP    LM, 0, D
        WAITD   1                       ; tick 7: low until the bit's end
        CMPI    r3, 0                   ; fetch the next bit into r6
        BNZ     dfa
        SUBI    r5, 1
        BZ      dfe
        ADDI    r1, 1
        LD      r2, r1, 0
        LDI     r3, 9
dfa:    MOV     r6, r2
        ANDI    r6, 1
        SHRI    r2, 1
        SUBI    r3, 1
        JMP     dfd
dfe:    LDI     r6, 2                   ; none: the end (F)
dfd:    CMPI    r6, 1
        BZ      dd
        WAITD   9                       ; the next bit's start
        JMP     nb
dd:     SETP    LM, 1, D
        WAITD   9                       ; a D: its first rise
        JMP     dbit

; the next bit's start, no subcarrier: an E, or the end
nb:     CMPI    r6, 0
        BNZ     tend
        CMPI    r3, 0                   ; E: fetch the bit after it
        BNZ     efa
        SUBI    r5, 1
        BZ      efe
        ADDI    r1, 1
        LD      r2, r1, 0
        LDI     r3, 9
efa:    MOV     r6, r2
        ANDI    r6, 1
        SHRI    r2, 1
        SUBI    r3, 1
        JMP     efd
efe:    LDI     r6, 2
efd:    SETP    LM, 1, D
        WAITD   8                       ; tick 8: the second half's first rise
        SETP    LM, 0, D
        WAITD   1
        SETP    LM, 1, D
        WAITD   1
        SETP    LM, 0, D
        WAITD   1
        SETP    LM, 1, D
        WAITD   1
        SETP    LM, 0, D
        WAITD   1
        SETP    LM, 1, D
        WAITD   1
        SETP    LM, 0, D
        WAITD   1                       ; tick 15
        CMPI    r6, 1
        BZ      ed
        WAITD   1                       ; tick 16: the next bit's start
        JMP     nb
ed:     SETP    LM, 1, D                ; E then D: one tick to the rise
        WAITD   1
        JMP     dbit

tend:   LDI     r7, 0                   ; F: the line stays low
        CSRW    TICK_FRAC, r7
        LDI     r7, 1
        CSRW    TICK_INT, r7            ; tick = 1 clock again
        JMP     rx
